turnip: cached GPU mapping for host imports on an IO-coherent GPU

The caller's pages are write-back cached for the CPU. Where the kernel
reports the GPU IO-coherent, an import asks for the cached, shareable GPU
mapping that snoops the CPU caches; otherwise the GPU reads stale lines
and the CPU keeps them over what the GPU wrote.

--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_sweet.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_sweet.cc
@@ -177,6 +177,8 @@
    struct sgpu_import_user req = {
       .addr = (uintptr_t) ptr,
       .size = size,
+      /* the pages are cached for the CPU: an IO-coherent GPU snoops them */
+      .flags = dev->physical_device->has_cached_coherent_memory ? SGPU_MEM_CACHED : 0u,
    };
    int ret = sgpu_import_user(sweet_dev(dev), &req);
    if (ret) {
